<!doctype html><html><head><title>docs/auto-reasoning-effort.md</title></head><body><header><nav><a href="/">Home</a></nav></header><main><article class="markdown-body"><h1>Auto reasoning effort</h1>
<p>Auto reasoning effort sets how much a model thinks for each message and for
each step after a batch of tool results. Simple messages run at a lower
effort, and harder work runs higher, instead of every request running at one
fixed level. It is on by default and runs entirely on your machine.</p>
<h2>Results on Terminal-Bench 2.1</h2>
<p>On the same model, GPT-6.1 Sol at <code>xhigh</code>, Auto cut the cost by <strong>35%</strong> compared
with running every request at a fixed <code>xhigh</code>, at a near-equal score. All 89
tasks, one pass each (<code>k=1</code>), web search on, 2026-10-15, with effort judge v6
(the previous judge; v7 has not been run on the benchmark):</p>
<table>
